OL,3,GNEWSALeader 'confident' of dropping
OL,4,AClean Air Zone fees
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe leader of Bradford Council has said
OL,7,Fhis group remains "confident" it can
OL,8,Fscrap the city's Clean Air Zone (CAZ)
OL,9,Fcharges despite the "legalities" of the
OL,10,Fmove.
OL,12,FAs part of the initiative to improve
OL,13,Fair quality, commercial vehicles that
OL,14,Fcause the most pollution are currently
OL,15,Fcharged a daily fee to enter Bradford
OL,16,Fand parts of Shipley.
OL,18,FIn his first BBC interview since May,
OL,19,FReform UK's Stephen Place said he is
OL,20,Fstill committed to "stop charging
OL,21,Fpeople for driving their vehicles round
OL,22,Fthe city".
OL,23,APub: 08-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
